                "stats-run.json warnings: \"ValueWarning: Negative binomial dispersion parameter alpha not set. Using default value alpha=1.0.\""
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "A negative binomial model with fixed alpha=1.0 fails to capture overdispersion; standard errors, confidence intervals, and p-values are likely incorrect, rendering the analysis unreliable.",
              "actionableFix": "Re-run the negative binomial regression with maximum likelihood estimation of the dispersion parameter (e.g., in statsmodels use `NegativeBinomial(y, X, loglike_method='nb2')` and check convergence). Alternatively, compare with a Poisson model and assess need for overdispersion.",
              "reentryPoint": "execution",
              "deterministicVerification": null,
              "confidence": 0.99
